      {
        "id": "blue-smoke-means-oil-is-burning-never-normal",
        "title": "Blue Smoke Means Oil is Burning - Never Normal",
        "description": "Blue or grey smoke from the exhaust means your engine is burning oil. Oil enters the combustion chamber through three main routes:",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Valve stem seals (£500-£1,500)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Oil leaks past worn seals when the engine is off. Smoke appears on start-up."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Piston rings (£1,500-£4,000+)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Worn rings allow oil past the pistons. Smoke appears under acceleration."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Turbo seals (£450-£3,000+)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Oil passes through failing turbo bearings. Smoke appears constantly."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "📊 In our 24,650 quote dataset, 55% of blue smoke cases were piston rings , 30% were valve stem seals, and 15% were turbo seals. The critical diagnostic clue is WHEN the smoke appears."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What people think vs reality"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "blue-smoke-means-oil-is-burning-never-normal",
          "order": 1
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "the-expensive-mistake-is-assuming-blue-smoke-is-harmless",
        "title": "The Expensive Mistake is Assuming Blue Smoke is Harmless",
        "description": "Understand why ignoring oil combustion triggers catastrophic emissions and engine failures.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "cards",
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "",
                "text": "“A little blue smoke is normal in older cars.” Any blue smoke means oil is burning. It's never normal and always needs investigation.",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "“A little blue smoke is normal in older cars.” Any blue smoke means oil is burning. It's never normal and always needs investigation."
              },
              {
                "title": "",
                "text": "“I'll just keep topping up the oil.” You're masking the problem. Burning oil damages your catalytic converter and DPF (£500-£2,000 replacements).",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "“I'll just keep topping up the oil.” You're masking the problem. Burning oil damages your catalytic converter and DPF (£500-£2,000 replacements)."
              },
              {
                "title": "",
                "text": "“It's just the turbo; I can replace it.” If you smoke on acceleration only, it's piston rings - not the turbo. Get diagnosed first.",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "“It's just the turbo; I can replace it.” If you smoke on acceleration only, it's piston rings - not the turbo. Get diagnosed first."
              },
              {
                "title": "",
                "text": "“An oil change will fix it.” No. Oil changes don't fix mechanical wear. The smoke will return within days.",
                "highlight": "",
                "meta": "",
                "icon": "",
                "items": [],
                "fullText": "“An oil change will fix it.” No. Oil changes don't fix mechanical wear. The smoke will return within days."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Blue smoke types & repair costs"
          }
        ],
        "links": [],
        "source": {
          "sectionId": "the-expensive-mistake-is-assuming-blue-smoke-is-harmless",
          "order": 2
        }
