      {
        "id": "diagnosis-first-quote-second",
        "title": "Diagnosis First, Quote Second",
        "description": "Follow this 3-step triage to isolate mechanical wear accurately.",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Step 1: Monitor oil consumption Check oil level weekly. Note how much you're adding (litres per 1,000 miles). If exceeding 0.5L per 1,000 miles = concerning.",
              "Step 2: Note smoke timing When does it appear? (cold start, acceleration, constant). This determines the likely cause.",
              "Step 3: Book professional diagnostic (£50-£150) A technician will perform a compression test, test cylinder leak-down, inspect turbo for oil leaks, and check for oil in the intake system."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Book Diagnostic"
          },
